#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:1
msgid "ABI tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:3
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:5
msgid ""
"This text tries to describe gcc semantic for mangling \"abi_tag\" attributes "
"described in <https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/C_002b_002b-Attributes.html>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:8
msgid ""
"There is no guarantee the following rules are correct, complete or make "
"sense in any way as they were determined empirically by experiments with "
"gcc5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:11
msgid "Declaration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:13
msgid ""
"ABI tags are declared in an abi_tag attribute and can be applied to a "
"function, variable, class or inline namespace declaration. The attribute "
"takes one or more strings (called tags); the order does not matter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:17
msgid ""
"See <https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/C_002b_002b-Attributes.html> for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:20
msgid ""
"Tags on an inline namespace are called \"implicit tags\", all other tags are "
"\"explicit tags\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:23
msgid "Mangling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:25
msgid ""
"All tags that are \"active\" on an `<unqualified-name>` are emitted after "
"the `<unqualified-name>`, before `<template-args>` or `<discriminator>`, and "
"are part of the same `<substitution>` the `<unqualified-name>` is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:29
msgid "They are mangled as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:36 ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:68
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:44
msgid "Active tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:46
msgid ""
"A namespace does not have any active tags. For types (class / struct / "
"union / enum), the explicit tags are the active tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:49
msgid ""
"For variables and functions, the active tags are the explicit tags plus any "
"\"required tags\" which are not in the \"available tags\" set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:57
msgid "Required tags for a function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:59
msgid ""
"If a function is used as a local scope for another name, and is part of "
"another function as local scope, it doesn't have any required tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:62
msgid ""
"If a function is used as a local scope for a guard variable name, it doesn't "
"have any required tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:65
msgid ""
"Otherwise the function requires any implicit or explicit tag used in the "
"name for the return type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:80
msgid "Required tags for a variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:82
msgid "A variable requires any implicit or explicit tag used in its type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:84
msgid "Available tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:86
msgid ""
"All tags used in the prefix and in the template arguments for a name are "
"available. Also, for functions, all tags from the `<bare-function-type>` "
"(which might include the return type for template functions) are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:90
msgid ""
"For `<local-name>`s all active tags used in the local part (`<function-"
"encoding>`) are available, but not implicit tags which were not active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:94
msgid ""
"Implicit and explicit tags used in the `<unqualified-name>` for a function "
"(as in the type of a cast operator) are NOT available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ItaniumMangleAbiTags.md:97
msgid ""
"Example: a cast operator to std::string (which is `std::__cxx11::"
"basic_string<...>`) will use 'cxx11' as an active tag, as it is required "
"from the return type `std::string` but not available."
msgstr ""
